WEBVTT

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.750
Ah! My Goddess
Flights of Fancy

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:23.280
In this wide world

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:28.460
People you're meant to meet can be seen

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:35.030
Beyond the window, beyond the rainbow

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:38.660
I think you're aware of them

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.780
Take off that restrictive weight

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.740
Let your feelings go

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:56.050
Now keep your ears open and wait for that time

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.820
Awaken now

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:12.100
Cherish the little dream you've
drawn in the vast sky

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:19.380
If you do, you can always become happy

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.140
It's certain

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.510
Woh woh

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:43.600
Morisato...

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.540
Morisato...

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:54.910
Who's there?

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.010
Keima?

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:01.750
I mean, Hotarunosuke.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.990
What is "destiny"?

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:20.100
Ever since I met Belldandy,
I've wondered that from time to time.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:24.770
Perhaps the dream I had that night had
been a sign of something to come.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.370
Keiichi?

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:30.680
Are you up?

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:31.980
Yeah...

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.510
Good morning, Keiichi!

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.380
Morning, Belldandy... Huh?

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.520
Hiking Journal
Hotarunosuke Morisato

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.080
Hiking Journal
Hotarunosuke Morisato
This is...

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:49.130
Ah! Everyone Has a Destiny!

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.770
I found this when I was going
through some boxes recently.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:54.270
Hiking Journal
Hotarunosuke Morisato

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.440
Hiking Journal
Hotarunosuke Morisato
It's my grandfather's journal!

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.540
Hiking Journal
Hotarunosuke Morisato
Huh...

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.110
Huh...

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.700
So his name was Hotarunosuke, huh?

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.880
He was more handsome than you.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.710
Aw, can it.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:08.380
Who's that in the picture with him?

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:13.190
Hmm... The photo's a little worn,
I can't make her out very well.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.160
Maybe it's my grandma, Machiko?

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.260
A map!

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:19.400
There's something written on it.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.200
"My life's luster... has been left here"?

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.130
It's a...
"My life's luster... has been left here"?

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:23.690
It's a...

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.270
What could it mean?

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:28.540
Okay, Keiichi! We're ready to go!

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.170
Huh? Go what?

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:34.280
Whenever there's an X on a map,
it's obvious it means there's treasure!

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.210
A magnificent adventure awaits us!

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.550
You guys watch too much TV.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:43.550
Look, the Auto Club's camping trip
is right around the corner,

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.860
so I don't have the time or the money.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.490
Oh, boo! You suck!

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.430
Say what you like, it doesn't make...

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.360
Oh, Morisato!

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:54.760
Hey!

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:05.600
And so, let the Nekomi Tech Auto Club's
Power Up Camping Trip begin!

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:10.170
Why are you here, too?

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.540
Isn't it obvious? 'Cuz it looked like fun.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.150
I thought you'd say that...

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.550
What, are you saying you have
some problem with the sponsor

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.220
who generously funded this trip?

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.460
None...

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.020
Very well, then.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:25.930
Anyhow, this sure is a stylish mansion.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.870
I heard the owner was an
acquaintance of my grandfather's.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:34.600
When I called, he said we could
rent the place out cheap.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.880
Do you feel it, Belldandy?

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:43.280
I do, Urd. I feel a presence.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.870
There's something in there.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:53.150
Hello? This is Morisato...

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.650
There is something here.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.730
If it's a demon...

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.820
...I'll take it down!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.600
I've been waiting for you.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.870
Welcome to Honda Manor.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:17.840
I have been appointed to take care of you,
my name is Chieko Honda.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:19.710
H... Huh?

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:21.880
W-We're in your debt.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.080
Uh... Thanks for your help.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.930
Oh, Master Morisato!

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.330
HUH?!

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:35.970
You remembered our promise, didn't you?

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:37.400
I'm so happy...

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.700
Um, what exactly are you talking about?

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.170
Morisato!

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.910
You sonnuva...

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:49.470
Well, well. You stud, you.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.920
When you already have my big sister...

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.150
You dirtbag!

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:55.480
Y-You're mistaken! This is some kind of...
You dirtbag!

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.780
Y-You're mistaken! This is some kind of...

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:07.530
It can't be. Then... you've truly
forgotten our promise?

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:11.690
Promise? But this is the
first time I've MET you!

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.800
Have you forgotten me, too?!

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:18.270
Forgotten you? Well, I mean...

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:18.910
Yeow!

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:19.940
I'm sorry! Are you okay?
Yeow!

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:22.140
I'm sorry! Are you okay?

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:27.440
E-Excuse me, but could you tell me
exactly what YOUR relationship is?

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:32.290
Huh? Our relationship? Well...

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:38.190
In... In any case, we made a promise
with each other a long time ago!

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:41.090
Uh, I'm kind of at a loss here...

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:43.230
Morisato!

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.200
It's time for our meeting.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.610
Aren't you finished with your
lovers' quarrel yet?

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.940
I don't know if that's what you'd call it...

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:55.780
Look, it's getting dark already, so why don't
we just leave it at that for today?

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:58.410
Then I shall get your dinner
ready right away.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:00.310
I'll be glad to help out.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.180
No thank you.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:08.120
She's a remnant.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:11.290
Yes... I know that, Urd.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.160
Then why aren't we doing anything?

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.500
There's something that concerns me.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:16.960
Wait a minute!

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.330
What's a remnant?

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:24.870
When someone departs this world

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:27.170
and leaves behind a strong
emotional sentiment,

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:31.070
those feelings can take on a physical form.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.610
That's what a remnant is.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.790
Is... Is she a g-ghost?!

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:40.260
Well, something like that, I guess.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:42.090
I'm going home!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:49.100
Let us begin the Auto Club's Camping
Trip Meeting! Go ahead, Dai-chan.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:50.070
Right.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.690
Number 36, Otaki!
I'll be singing for you now!

00:07:56.240 --> 00:08:04.280
The blood in my veins is my gasoline!

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:08.650
I'll put my life on the line
and blast forward!

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:12.480
My soul is a burned engine!

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:18.060
I'm gonna drink myself into oblivion!

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:31.610
Are you okay?

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:34.470
You've had a lot to drink.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:37.080
Why not take a little rest?

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:46.160
I can't remember, no matter how much I try.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:50.460
Have I really made some kind
of promise with you?

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.000
Where did you get a copy of that photo?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.630
Who the heck... are you...

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.080
Was it just my imagination?

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:13.050
Hey, Bell... are you listening?

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:14.050
Yes.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:20.010
So I've decided to open my own shop
and make it on my own!

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.860
These are good...

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:27.090
Here! You wanna try one, too?

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.560
Okay, thank you.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.500
The seasoning in these potatoes...

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:41.510
Hey, Morisato, where are ya?

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:46.240
You, like, makin' out with
Belldandy or somethin'?

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.350
You've had a little too much to drink!

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:51.720
You just saw Big Sister with
the others a minute ago!

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.070
Skuld!

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:11.100
Urd!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:14.240
I can't find the remnant or Keiichi! Come on!

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:15.340
Okay!

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:20.480
Yeah!
All right!

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:21.680
Way to go!
Nice job!

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:22.840
Aw, hell yeah!

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:35.460
We should never have let them
out of our sight.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:38.060
She's going to possess Keiichi!

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:39.700
It couldn't be.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.040
Don't be naive!

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.300
A remnant will do anything it takes
to achieve what it's after.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.870
Skuld! Hasegawa!

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:48.910
This is the room, isn't it?

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:50.540
They've only passed out.

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:54.750
My unbinding spell doesn't work.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.240
Hey! Open this door!

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:01.860
We know you're in there!

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:03.990
Give it up and come out here now!

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:07.120
It's no use. That door will not open.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:14.630
Now... please remember that day
and the promise we made.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:17.870
Please fulfill your promise.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:24.680
Ah! Ghosts!

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:26.550
Look who's talking!

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:32.790
That won't work. Remnants are
not the same as demons,

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.850
so the usual anti-demonic
programs won't work.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:43.960
Please, grant my wish. I'll never
let go of you until you do.

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:48.390
Stop it! Do you really not know who he is?

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:52.500
NO!

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:57.510
That is Keiichi you have!

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:01.620
It's not Hotarunosuke, the one
you've been waiting for!

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:06.980
That doesn't matter! It doesn't...

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:13.790
My encounter with Master Hotarunosuke
lasted only four summer days.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:17.630
I met him while I was being
treated for an illness,

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.400
and he made a promise to me.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:26.800
Even when I was on my sickbed,
that promise gave me strength.

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:33.880
When I had left this world, I still waited.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.920
And then he came to see me.

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:43.310
Even though it is a different era,
he was guided by fate.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:50.090
Please tell me... what the promise
you made with Hotarunosuke was.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:06.580
Huh? What am I doing in bed?

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:10.450
Good morning, Keiichi!

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:15.680
There's something I'd like you
to have a look at.

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:26.830
What would you want to show me
down here in the basement?

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:30.000
Huh?! You're...

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.910
And... This is...

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:35.810
A Brough Superior!

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:39.480
But, what's it doing in a place like this?

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.090
It couldn't be!

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:48.290
Yes. It seems it broke down
and was left here.

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:52.490
This bike was your grandfather's. And...

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:56.530
I'd like you to please repair it.

00:13:56.930 --> 00:14:01.140
I don't mind if you take it
after you've fixed it.

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:07.810
Just, before that take me for
a ride around the lake on it.

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:11.870
That was Master Hotarunosuke's promise.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.680
You've waited decades, just for that...

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:19.250
You waited here the whole time, didn't you?

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:24.320
Just your words are comfort for me.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.430
Then the thing to do now is...

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.370
Th-This is...

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:35.770
The so-called "Rolls-Royce" of motorcycles!

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.170
It's a Brough Superior!

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:42.410
All right! Now we can rebuild
our club's finances!

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:45.580
It's a treasure! Treasure!
It's definitely worth repairing!

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:46.410
This is a chance to show what we got!

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:48.050
This is a chance to show what we got!
It's these guys that are going
to be the problem.

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:48.910
It's these guys that are going
to be the problem.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:50.550
Excuse me!

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:55.310
Allow me to fix this bike on my own.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:59.230
What did you say?
Morisato, you rat, don't tell me...

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:01.820
You're not thinking you'll hog it
all to yourself, are you?!

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:03.560
Keep your mouths shut!

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:08.130
So why do you need to fix it all on your own?

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:15.240
Yes, well... I must fix this bike on my own.

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:17.380
It is my destiny.

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:19.050
Destiny, huh?

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:21.150
Guess there's no arguing then.

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:22.550
Tamiya, Otaki!

00:15:22.550 --> 00:15:23.680
Yes, ma'am!

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:26.960
My chronic abdominal spasms!

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:29.010
Are you okay, Den-chan?!

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:31.450
C'mon, this way.

00:15:32.060 --> 00:15:33.860
Wh-What was that?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:39.770
Those guys... where were they
hiding all that on them?

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:41.100
Morisato.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:45.770
Just about every motorcycle from this
generation is like a unique model unto itself.

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:48.240
They've got a lot of peculiarities, so watch out.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:49.270
Okay.

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:50.710
Well, see ya later.

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:53.540
Th-Thank you very much!

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.320
How long are you gonna sulk over this?

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:03.390
Well, it's totally embarrassing for a goddess to
let herself faint after seeing a mere remnant...

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:06.090
Don't let it get to you!

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:09.830
Sure you're a "goddess,"
but you're only a kid, after all.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:12.870
WHAT'S YOUR PROBLEM?
WHY DON'T YOU JUST SHUT UP?!

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:15.300
I HATE YOU, URD!

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.000
Yeah, yeah.

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:21.800
So how's he doing?

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:26.580
Say, there's one thing I don't get.

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:32.880
How did you know she had a connection
with Keiichi's grandfather?

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:36.560
Because of the seasoning
on her nice taters.

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:37.760
"Taters"?

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:41.230
The flavor of the boiled potatoes she served

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:45.970
was exactly the same as the
seasoning recipe Megumi gave me.

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:48.660
So it was the "Morisato flavor," huh?

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:52.970
His grandfather's photo and
map tipped me off, too.

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:54.800
That's just like you.

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:59.410
Oh, dear. Aren't you worried?

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:02.280
At this rate, she'll steal Keiichi from you.

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:06.880
I think I understand how she feels.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:11.450
Someday, Keiichi and I will also...

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.560
Belldandy!

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:17.800
C'mon, RUN!

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:20.270
Give me one more lap.

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:22.370
I'm gonna croak!

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:24.570
Those two are totally spent.

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:25.900
I don't believe it...

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:28.610
Oh, leave me alone!

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:30.040
Aw, c'mon!

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:33.150
Hey, you don't have many channels here.

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:34.810
You're interfering with my cleaning!

00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:38.150
The laundry will dry nicely today.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.760
Please take a little break.

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:41.950
Thanks.

00:17:42.520 --> 00:17:45.290
Why should a goddess have to do push-ups?

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.400
Now you add the heavy cream.

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:50.760
I see...

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.330
This is more efficient.

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:57.140
It seems that this part is hurting.

00:17:57.140 --> 00:17:58.500
I see.

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.250
Okay, all done.

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:11.390
Now we'll be able to take it
for that ride tomorrow.

00:18:11.390 --> 00:18:13.250
Oh, good work!

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:16.930
Say, can I ask you a question?

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.090
What is it?

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:23.630
I think Hotarunosuke really did
want to come here.

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:26.370
But he couldn't in the end.

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:31.510
And because of that, you've ended up
waiting here for decades.

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:35.640
Do you ever think it would have been
better if you'd never met him at all?

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:41.140
When I was sick in bed, I did feel
some resentment towards him.

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:44.620
I wondered why he wouldn't come to see me.

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:49.860
But even despite that, my
meeting Hotarunosuke

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:55.530
was the brightest moment of my life.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:19:00.500
That's why I'm sure it's far better to have
met him and suffered this fate,

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:05.240
than to have passed him by and
never known him at all.

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:09.540
I guess I'll know after tomorrow's ride
whether I was right or wrong.

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:21.360
Well, we'll be back in a bit.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:22.420
Okay.

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:24.220
Be careful, okay?

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:27.930
Well, there they go.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:29.060
Yes.

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.340
Here, have a look.

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:54.820
The soft breeze...
The pleasant hum of the engine...

00:19:56.420 --> 00:20:00.730
And scenery from a completely
different perspective

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:02.660
than when you just walk along the road.

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:05.100
This is what you wanted to show me,

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:07.230
back when I feared death as it loomed.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:12.230
That the trees, the land, the sky...

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:14.440
And me...

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:18.110
That we all share a common destiny,

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:21.740
in how we'll be swept away in
an instant on this breeze...

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:28.790
But... That's the very reason I'm
so happy I could meet you.

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:37.460
On this breeze that blows only here
and now, Master Hotarunosuke...

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:40.430
Thank you...

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:44.700
For putting up with my selfish demands.

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:49.100
It's not like that! I...

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:06.950
"Goodbye." I felt as though that's what
I heard at the very last moment.

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:11.500
Our treasure, it...
Oh, Den-chan!

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.000
You two stop crying!
You're supposed to be adults!

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:14.800
Are you really going to leave it here?
You two stop crying!
You're supposed to be adults!

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:15.140
Are you really going to leave it here?

00:21:15.140 --> 00:21:16.070
Yeah.

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:20.680
I saw myself in her, that's all.

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:26.380
There might come a time when I'll be
like that, waiting for Belldandy.

00:21:27.520 --> 00:21:29.070
Keiichi...

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:34.980
That's why I'd like to at least leave
the bike here. For her...

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:42.460
I won't keep you waiting for years and years.

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:44.530
Ah, that's a relief!

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:48.300
I've been wondering for the longest time
what I'd do if that ever happens.

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:50.200
What WOULD you do?

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:55.910
I'd just work on my bike,
and keep on waiting for you.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:22:00.900
And if we were to meet again,
I'd take you for a ride.

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:05.420
You and so many others I've met...

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:07.550
The whole town of Nekomi.

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:13.590
Keiichi... I'm glad we came here.

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:18.870
And so, in the basement of the
old hotel on the hilltop,

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:24.030
you can still find a Brough Superior
motorcycle continuing to sleep the time away.

00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:34.820
Whenever one day ends

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:47.800
"I loved you again today,"
I think quietly in my heart

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:51.930
When I think back, you see

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:57.310
There were days when I
wore myself out crying

00:22:57.310 --> 00:23:06.150
But the place we reached after I
survived many such nights

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:10.550
And the story that began

00:23:10.550 --> 00:23:16.860
Is real in a somehow dreamlike way

00:23:16.860 --> 00:23:25.130
Premonitions of immeasurable love
were certainly overflowing

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:35.710
From our clasped hands even as we
laughed bashfully a little

00:23:35.710 --> 00:23:45.190
After all, beyond a doubt,
undeniably, you and I

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:50.210
Are in love with each other

00:23:55.660 --> 00:23:58.400
That's right, I'd be glad to tell you any time,

00:23:58.400 --> 00:24:01.990
letting the melody carry my infinite
feelings to you, b-but...

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:04.740
Next time: "Ah! The Song of Love
That Shakes the Heart!"

00:24:04.740 --> 00:24:05.570
Ah! The Song of Love That Shakes the Heart!
Next time: "Ah! The Song of Love
That Shakes the Heart!"

00:24:05.570 --> 00:24:06.510
Ah! The Song of Love That Shakes the Heart!
I love you!

00:24:06.510 --> 00:24:07.340
Ah! The Song of Love That Shakes the Heart!
L-L-L...

00:24:07.340 --> 00:24:09.510
Ah! The Song of Love That Shakes the Heart!
Oh, for Heaven's sake SPIT IT OUT!
